body: "Daily Release reconcile stops with `Live publication identity disagrees` before publishing or Bun verification. This recurs on two different default heads: [run 44537640577 / job 135607202342](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/actions/runs/44537640577/job/135607202342) at `6e67e50b`, and [run 44546195607 / job 135637302942](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/actions/runs/44546195607/job/135637302942) at `b4882442`. Both use the reusable workflow at `7687a35d7522482bd8361d60dbc2589e9afbc81c`.\n\nThe [merged release candidate #12](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/pull/12) targets npm `pm-reduce@2026.11.6` (Git tag `v2026.11.06`, source merge `4eca4d796f11904ca729c39df0dfc22d365d7148`). Its preparation receipt records SRI `sha512-wMC2ad8iWksWNZnqOH2vs1W8adaoSORhTbYNnIwRsb+TQuxfDDix1nb8/w6LvFdAm4qAvfcAz3w5F5Kl0O6TeA==`. The [official npm coordinate](https://registry.npmjs.org/pm-reduce/2026.11.6) is already occupied with different SRI `sha512-cp7w7enJ0yLB8Wkn7SgQum1wm3OfVIYnquHakz1aYWSGdKFtMQNjokZojTN9yy+diB2IyyT9UJ4uxeGmrb+z+Q==`. It was published November 15 at 19:45:12 UTC, before the candidate merged November 16 at 17:27:40 UTC. Registry metadata exposes no attestation, and the exact padded Git tag and GitHub Release REST lookups return 404.\n\nThe [pinned registry proof](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/blob/7687a35d7522482bd8361d60dbc2589e9afbc81c/scripts/release-continuation.ts#L151-L160) treats the digest mismatch as unverified, which the [continuation decision](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/blob/7687a35d7522482bd8361d60dbc2589e9afbc81c/release-continuation.ts#L150-L152) must reject. This is an occupied-coordinate mismatch, not evidence of a bad npm Trusted Publisher setting, signer SAN mismatch, or package compromise. Re-running unchanged cannot repair it. Distinct from unbraind/pm-ops#270; related rollout: unbraind/pm-ops#272 and [native rollout task](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/blob/b48824420f34da8034c747932d1b53b670728c3a/.agents/pm/tasks/reduce-pm-reduce-release-caller-rollout.toon).\n\n**Expected / acceptance:** Keep the artifact mismatch fail-closed. Record an operator-reviewed disposition for the stale occupied intent, then prepare current source as a fresh candidate at an unused npm version through the approved flow. Do not unpublish, overwrite, backfill a tag against mismatched bytes, relax provenance, or treat this as absent. Verify protected candidate CI and exact npm/GitHub digest, source/signer provenance, tag, release and Bun install for the eventual new version. On recurrence, report occupied/digest mismatch distinctly from a pending attempt or a verifier outage.\n\nEvidence is exact read-only CI, public registry metadata and immutable source; no release transitions or provider settings changed.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-19T19:32:07Z)\n>\n> Verified recovery milestone after [#22](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/pull/22) pinned `pm-ops` 2026.11.19. On exact main `e0efc3ef761ea08a9c0d8163dcf0fcab7a4ee498`, [the post-merge reconciliation job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/actions/runs/44598499036/job/135823200795) passed and reported that the candidate targeting the pre-existing `pm-reduce@2026.11.6` coordinate was retired for fresh preparation, with npm and tags left untouched. The [same run](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/actions/runs/44598499036) entered fresh preparation; no new publication or successful Bun verification had been observed at this checkpoint. This confirms the original reconciliation block cleared, not that end-to-end release is complete.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-19T20:25:39Z)\n>\n> End-to-end recovery verified: fresh [release PR #23](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/pull/23) merged at `921ec79dcb0d7d2f931f4475a5228ac3c08bf3f2` and produced [`pm-reduce@2026.11.19`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/releases/tag/v2026.11.19). [Run 44603579557](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-reduce/actions/runs/44603579557) completed with release and Bun verification green. Official npm `latest` is 2026.11.19; downloaded tarball matched its npm SHA-1 and SRI, and recorded provenance subject digest and source commit align with the tag. In a disposable no-Git tracker on official PM CLI 2026.11.19, the published package loaded and `reduce create`, `next`, and `packet` all succeeded on a synthetic fixture. The old occupied coordinate was not overwritten."
